CommitDate: Thu Nov 5 10:45:21 2026 -0500

    feat(git): make the commit/push write path visible (OBSDB-004)
    
    A namespace could stop reaching its remote while /health and every read stayed
    green: each failure was a console.warn that was swallowed, and the in-flight
    commit chains (asyncChains) were a Map size nothing read.
    
    src/git/metrics.ts now owns four spec §3.2 families — duckbrain_git_commit_total
    and duckbrain_git_push_total (outcome=ok|fail, outcome is the ONLY label, never
    a namespace), duckbrain_git_commit_queue_depth (a collect callback sampling
    asyncChains.size, so no interval holds a CLI process open) and
    duckbrain_git_last_push_success_timestamp_seconds (stamped only by a real
    success, so a broken remote freezes it while the fail counter climbs).
    autocommit.ts records at each real operation — commit counted where the commit
    ends (a failed push cannot look like a failed commit), push counted only when
    `git push` was actually invoked (gate skips and unchanged-HEAD short-circuits
    are not pushes) — and installs the depth sampler; src/http/metrics.ts attaches
    the process-wide instances to each scrape registry.
    
    Tests: unit label/sampling discipline, and end to end through createHttpServer
    with a file:// bare remote — one POSTed memory commits+pushes, a broken remote
    increments fail while the remote receives nothing and the stamp stays frozen,
    and a burst reads depth>0 in flight, 0 after. Suite 255 files / 2117 tests.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
